Z||000000||Loki||11-06-2001||09:57 PM||||Can an IP be traced from an e-mail? Im having ALOT of problems with me and my ex (mother of my son) and want to know if I can trace her or not.<P><P>------------------<BR>Loki<BR>"All Fieros broke right now" :(||||reg||1
Z||000001||Mach10||11-06-2001||10:05 PM||||Yep... "View Source" will give you most of the routing information, originator, domain, and yes, IP address.<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000002||Loki||11-06-2001||10:29 PM||||Of course its something simple   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>THANX<P>------------------<BR>Loki<BR>"All Fieros broke right now" :(||||reg||1
Z||000003||thomas_l||11-07-2001||10:00 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Mach10:<BR><B>Yep... "View Source" will give you most of the routing information, originator, domain, and yes, IP address.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well... it really depends on the ISP. Some will include the originating user ID or IP in their headers but not many. Even with the IP, you need to confirm who was using it at the time the message was sent due to most ISPs using dynamic addressing. You will most likely narrow it down to the originating SMTP (sendmail) server and a message-ID. From there you would probably need a court order for the SMTP server owner to release details of exactly who sent the message.<P>Your best recourse outside of a criminal warrant would be to forward the nasty-grams to the originating ISP's abuse desk. Look at their web site to find the address, or roll the dice by forwarding to "abuse@host_isp_goes_here" or "postmaster@host_isp_goes_here" or "support@host_isp_goes_here". If you get lucky they will agree you are being harassed and zap the offending user account  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||3
Z||000004||loafer87gt||11-07-2001||10:17 AM||||Download the demo version of a program of Neotrace. You can copy the information from the email header into it and it will tell you where the email was sent from. If you can get the IP adress of the sender it will even give you a map of the city and the location of where the sender sent the email from. Tres cool. I managed to track down some hacker from the University of Indiana using the program. The program tracked the hacker to the University, told me which station the computer # at the school the kid was using, and even gave the me the email address for the person in charge of security. Here is the addy:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.neoworx.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.neoworx.com/</A> ||||reg||1
